{"lines": ["In July nineteen sixty-nine, a ship found a racing yacht drifting in the middle of the Atlantic.", "Nobody was aboard.", "It was the Tin-muth Electron, sailed alone by Donald Crowhurst in a race around the world.", "For months, his radio reports had put him far ahead.", "Newspapers said he might win.", "But his logbooks were still on board.", "They told a different story.", "He never left the Atlantic.", "For seven months, he wandered the South Atlantic and radioed fake positions.", "He even stopped secretly in Argentina, which broke the rules.", "Then his final pages turned into twenty-five thousand words of strange philosophy.", "The last entry, on July first, ended with four words.", "'It is the mercy.'", "The chronometer case was found empty.", "His body was never found.", "So what happened on that empty deck?", "Nobody explained it."], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.1], ["July", 0.1, 0.24], ["nineteen", 0.24, 0.682], ["sixty-nine,", 0.682, 1.18], ["a", 1.9, 2.06], ["ship", 2.06, 2.26], ["found", 2.26, 2.62], ["a", 2.62, 2.76], ["racing", 2.76, 3.08], ["yacht", 3.08, 3.38], ["drifting", 3.38, 3.72], ["in", 3.72, 4.1], ["the", 4.1, 4.16], ["middle", 4.16, 4.38], ["of", 4.38, 4.54], ["the", 4.54, 4.64], ["Atlantic.", 4.64, 4.96], ["Nobody", 5.541, 5.76], ["was", 5.76, 6.12], ["aboard.", 6.12, 6.38], ["It", 6.96, 7.04], ["was", 7.04, 7.18], ["the", 7.18, 7.34], ["Tin-muth", 7.34, 7.84], ["Electron,", 7.84, 8.32], ["sailed", 8.84, 9.08], ["alone", 9.08, 9.48], ["by", 9.48, 9.76], ["Donald", 9.76, 10.02], ["Crowhurst", 10.02, 10.72], ["in", 10.72, 10.88], ["a", 10.88, 10.96], ["race", 10.96, 11.16], ["around", 11.16, 11.48], ["the", 11.48, 11.66], ["world.", 11.66, 11.92], ["For", 12.44, 12.7], ["months,", 12.7, 12.92], ["his", 13.3, 13.4], ["radio", 13.4, 13.7], ["reports", 13.7, 14.08], ["had", 14.08, 14.36], ["put", 14.36, 14.52], ["him", 14.52, 14.66], ["far", 14.66, 14.88], ["ahead.", 14.88, 15.2], ["Newspapers", 15.64, 16.16], ["said", 16.16, 16.5], ["he",